Rejig: write a configured widget back under its element id. Applies to ios_homescreen/state.py from
https://github.com/YakupEmreYerli/ios-homescreen at commit
97649547dbc44295e451c6bf130a87404481e10c, after Rejig's other patches. A configured single
widget shows its element id only as userSelectedElementIdentifier; the write now sends it
as uniqueIdentifier too, so SpringBoard keeps the widget under that id instead of a fresh
one that, per homescreen-mcp, orphans its settings. Stacks keep their keys as read (there the key names the
element on show). Readback takes a single widget's id from uniqueIdentifier, else
userSelectedElementIdentifier, and lets a missing id pass, since iOS drops it from some
reads; two different ids still fail. Fingerprints keep the exact id. Method from homescreen-mcp
(https://github.com/kats1123/homescreen-mcp, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Jonathan Kats).
ios-homescreen is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2026 Yakup Emre Yerli (full notice in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). This patch is MIT.

